# Unity generated project files
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.slnx

# ...except the hand-written ones. Unity regenerates about seventy csproj files
# at the repo root, which is what the wildcards above are for, but these are
# maintained by hand and are the only way to build from a clone. The negations
# have to sit after the wildcards to take effect. MajdataEdit.csproj was being
# swallowed too, so the workflow that builds it was pointing at a file the repo
# did not contain.
!Tests/SlideAstRegression/SlideAstRegression.csproj
!MajdataEdit/MajdataEdit.csproj
!MajdataEdit/MajdataEdit.sln
!MajdataLauncher/MajdataLauncher.csproj
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

